WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:01.770
Speaker 1: We have a voicemail number.

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.239
That number is two one nine two.

00:00:03.239 --> 00:00:10.059
David, P. I am really, really, really regretting
something I did on the show two weeks ago.

00:00:10.059 --> 00:00:14.290
Now someone said, David, if you had to leave
the country, where would you go?

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:16.950
I have no plan to leave the country.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.570
I don't think it's going to be necessary to
leave the country.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:23.130
But I answered the question anyway, and I
said, Well, I could go back to Argentina any

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.400
time because I was born there, so I could.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:32.029
I can go anytime as a Jewish individual, I
could go to Israel at any time.

00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:38.360
I'm working on getting European citizenship
through my grandfather, who fled Poland before,

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.960
but I'm not planning to do any OK.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:45.980
The number of messages I have received now
from people saying, David, I'm canceling my

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:49.649
membership because I don't want to be with
someone who's going to abandon us if the going

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:53.460
gets tough, all these different things, I
regret even talking about it.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.970
And now this is sort of the height of it.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:01:04.960
This caller said, David, you planning to leave
makes you seem like the unpatriotic Jew who

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.920
will take his capital and leave with no loyalty.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:15.630
We've gotten to the anti-Semitic tropes part
of the leaving the country timeline.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:16.630
Take a listen to this.

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:19.290
Speaker 6: He gave my name is Jeff.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:24.200
I'm calling you about your recent segments
reference you leaving the United States.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:29.310
If things go with George Harrison, that raises
a couple of concerns.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:33.189
I think that were born out in Alex Jones's
response to those videos.

00:01:33.189 --> 00:01:39.780
The first concern is is that it reinforces
the trope the Jews aren't really patriotic

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:40.960
or good citizens.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:45.100
And here, you know, things get bad enough
to leave.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:50.240
Second concern is that promotes the trope
that, you know, Jews are global, said who

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:53.420
will pick up their capital and split for better
markets.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.549
The first sort of trouble.

00:01:55.549 --> 00:02:01.939
I'm saying this is a guy who by right may
go to Israel or may go to Spain, but I won't

00:02:01.939 --> 00:02:06.760
go to either one of those places, except and
only if I'm a tourist.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:10.920
If things get bad here, it's only because
we can get bad.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:19.170
Speaker 1: Guys, I'm not leaving in a true
dystopia, the likes of which I was imagining

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:22.900
when I answered the question, we would all
be looking to leave.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:24.360
There wouldn't be any more tourism.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:25.550
It would be an emergency.

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.810
We would all be looking for safe haven.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:30.170
Me being Jewish wouldn't change that.

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:35.190
This was the question asked by the audience
if you were to leave because things got so

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:36.340
bad.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:37.780
Where would you go?

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:40.080
And it's true if I left.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:45.890
I'm not going to go to Thailand or Norway,
where I both don't speak the language and

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:48.720
have no way to actually go to legally.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:53.840
If I left, I would be more likely to go to
Argentina because I was born there or to Israel

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.930
for legal reasons, but I'm not planning on
leaving.

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:03.490
And it was clearly a very big mistake to even
entertain the question.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:05.010
